TEXT 144 0 Left 3 ;#201 Reverse recovery, rectifier against switching diode
TEXT 144 64 Left 2 ;Source: Alan Wolke (W2AEW), https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=SBqLOrlA7QI
TEXT 144 112 Left 2 ;Alan's measurement fixture drawn twice, so a rectifier and a switching diode see the same pulse.
TEXT 144 816 Left 2 ;Each row is the fixture from Alan's notes page: a generator with its 50 ohm source resistance,
TEXT 144 848 Left 2 ;the device under test in series, and a 50 ohm termination at the scope. He draws the pulse
TEXT 144 880 Left 2 ;swinging between -1 V and +1 V, a few microseconds wide; the 5 ns edges stand for a generator.
TEXT 144 928 Left 2 ;The two devices are examples, not parts identified in the video. Both models are published by
TEXT 144 960 Left 2 ;Diodes Incorporated. A datasheet trr is specified at its own current and edge rate, so the
TEXT 144 992 Left 2 ;intervals measured here belong to this fixture and are not a datasheet qualification.
TEXT 840 224 Left 2 !.include ..\..\LTspice\Models\Diodes-Inc\DI_1N4007G.lib
TEXT 840 264 Left 2 !.include ..\..\LTspice\Models\Diodes-Inc\DI_1N4148W.lib
TEXT 840 304 Left 2 !.tran 0 5u 0 100p
TEXT 840 344 Left 2 !.options plotwinsize=0
TEXT 840 400 Left 2 !.meas tran if_slow AVG I(Dslow) FROM 3u TO 3.4u
TEXT 840 440 Left 2 !.meas tran irrm_slow MIN I(Dslow)
TEXT 840 480 Left 2 !.meas tran t0_slow WHEN I(Dslow)=0 CROSS=1 TD=3.5u
TEXT 840 520 Left 2 !.meas tran t10_slow WHEN I(Dslow)=-1m CROSS=2 TD=3.5u
TEXT 840 560 Left 2 !.meas tran trr_slow PARAM t10_slow-t0_slow
TEXT 840 616 Left 2 !.meas tran if_fast AVG I(Dfast) FROM 3u TO 3.4u
TEXT 840 656 Left 2 !.meas tran irrm_fast MIN I(Dfast)
